Package: rpass
Title: Native Client for 'pass'-Compatible Password Stores
Version: 0.0.2
Authors@R: person("Giuseppe", "Acito", email = "giuseppe.acito@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Read and manage entries in a password store compatible with
    'pass', the standard unix password manager <https://www.passwordstore.org/>,
    without shelling out to the 'pass' or 'gpg' binaries at runtime. OpenPGP
    parsing, decryption and encryption are implemented natively via the Rust
    'pgp' crate, embedded through 'extendr'/'rextendr'.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
SystemRequirements: Cargo (Rust's package manager), rustc >= 1.88
Imports:
    getPass,
    openssl,
    fs
Suggests:
    testthat (>= 3.0.0),
    withr
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Config/rextendr/version: 0.5.0
Depends:
    R (>= 4.2)
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.0.0
